# Build artifacts
/target

# Editor swap files
*.swp
*.swo

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

# Claude Code session data
.claude/

# Sort enum registry (generated at compile time by #[bsql::sort])
# Each enum writes its SQL fragments here for query! to validate.
# Regenerated on every build — not source-controlled.
.bsql/sorts/

# Examples crate has its own standalone cache that gets regenerated
# whenever someone runs `cargo run --bin <example>` locally. Not worth
# committing — the examples each validate against whatever DB the user
# has BSQL_DATABASE_URL pointed at.
examples/.bsql/

# Per-crate caches: rust-analyzer / cargo test inside a crate directory
# creates a `.bsql/` there too. Only the workspace-root `.bsql/queries/`
# is the canonical cache — committing per-crate directories would
# duplicate entries and confuse the manifest.
crates/*/.bsql/

TODO
*.txt

# The deps_pin gate's goldens ARE source of truth (like the trybuild
# `.stderr` goldens): they pin the resolved dependency set and the
# allowed version-duplications, and the gate fails on any drift. They
# must be committed despite the broad `*.txt` ignore above.
!tools/devgates/tests/deps_goldens/*.txt

# The next_event codegen gate's instruction-count ceiling is likewise a
# committed source-of-truth golden (regenerated with `BSQL_HOTPATH_PIN=overwrite`),
# so it too must survive the broad `*.txt` ignore above.
!crates/postgres/proto/tests/hotpath_goldens/*.txt